     "text": "FAX 1  ##\nEdwards Group Medical Group\nRe: Connor Ellis (DOB 05/27/1969)\n\nFebruary 10, 2025\n\nDear Sir or Madam,\n\nThis letter pertains to the medical status of Mr. Connor Ellis, born on May 27, 1969, who is under my care at Edwards Group Medical Group. \n\nMr. Ellis was seen on February 10, 2025, for a follow-up regarding his known Factor V Leiden mutation, which has been managed successfully. During this visit, his blood pressure was recorded at 115/79 mmHg, and his weight was 152 pounds. The patient remains stable and compliant with his treatment regimen for this condition, which includes anticoagulation therapy to mitigate the risk of venous thromboembolism. He has adhering to this therapy without complications. Additionally, Mr. Ellis reports that he continues to maintain an active lifestyle, running 3-4 times a week, and his exercise routine has remained consistent. Socially, he consumes alcohol a moderate level, averaging about four drinks per week.\n\nOn May 31, 2024, Mr. Ellis was seen for a routine follow-up visit concerning his Factor V Leiden mutation. At that his blood pressure was 107/85 mmHg, and he weighed 158 pounds. He continued to maintain stable health and has reported new issues related to his condition. His blood tests and clinical assessments have shown no signs of thromboembolic events, and his anticoagulation therapy remains effective.\n\nIn our visit on September 18, 2023, Mr. Ellis came in for a check-up regarding his Factor V Leiden mutation. His blood pressure was 108/85 mmHg, and his weight was 150 pounds. During this visit, Mr. Ellis reported feeling well overall and had no new complaints. His laboratory results and clinical evaluation were consistent with his previous assessments. The patient is compliant with his treatment and preventive measures, and he to follow a healthy lifestyle.\n\nMr. Ellis’s family history is pertinent as his father passed away at age 47 from a myocardial infarction, and his mother died at age 42 from sudden cardiac death. These events underscore the importance his ongoing medical and preventive strategies.\n\nIn summary, Mr. Ellis has been managing his Factor V Leiden mutation effectively with no recent complications. His blood pressure, weight, and overall health have remained stable throughout the follow-up visits. His active lifestyle and alcohol consumption are consistent with his otherwise healthy habits.\n\nThank you for considering this information. Should you require any additional details or have further questions, do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nSince"
